    "title": "feat(gateway): opt-in Jev-assessed reasoning seam for /answer + /brief (draft — handoff)",
    "body": "## Opt-in Jev-assessed reasoning seam for `/answer` + `/brief`\n\n**Draft — not for merge yet.** Opening per the handoff's recommended path (\"apply the patches, review, open draft PRs\"). The handoff states verbatim: *\"Do not treat this package as authorization to merge, publish or deploy.\"* Requesting @claude-warden review before anything lands.\n\n### What it adds\nA provider-independent, **opt-in** `deps.assessReasoning` loop wrapping the existing Gemma `reason`/`brief` drafting on `/answer` (grounded Q&A) and `/brief` (checkpoint briefing). New: `src/assessed-reasoning.mjs`, `src/reasoning-evidence.mjs`, `ASSESSMENT.md`, and tests. Key properties (read `services/pocket-gateway/ASSESSMENT.md`):\n\n- **No dial/tool/merge/governed-write capability.** `evaluated` = model-assessed *support*, not independently verified truth. An accepted briefing authorizes no action and does not alter the ring threshold.\n- **Spoken = displayed.** Each segment's spoken text must equal its validated text (`spoken-text-mismatch` otherwise) — the phone can't be slipped an alternate TTS payload.\n- **Honest confidence.** Absent model confidence stays `null` (never an invented `1.0`); a supplied finite rating is labeled model-self-reported-uncalibrated.\n- **Bounded, shared projection.** Drafting and assessment see the same ≤24 excerpts × 280 code points; required sources are selected first and rejected (not silently dropped) if they exceed budget.\n- **Bounded caller wait.** 2 attempts within a 10s budget; on any failure it returns honest failure metadata and **no generated prose**.\n- Signed-bundle canonical hash / contracts version / sequence range / signer identity bound into the assessment context (structural binding, not trust-anchor verification).\n\n### Provenance\nFrom the Jev/Pocket/Omar handoff (`pocket-jev-assessment.patch`), base `master@8f7f7927`. Authored commit carried in as-is; I am the reviewer, not the author.\n\n### Firsthand verification (pocket-forge)\n- Patch applies **clean** on current `master` (0 commits since base).\n- `node --test` in `services/pocket-gateway`: **897/897 runnable tests pass.** The only 3 non-passing are `gateway-entrypoint` / `operation-admission-entrypoint` / `registry-cutover-cli`, all failing `Cannot find package '@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb'` — a deploy dependency not installed in the local clone. **Control-tested on clean `master` without this patch: the same 3 fail identically.** The patch does not touch those files or that dependency.\n- Full suite runs in CI with the complete dep tree.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
